WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:03.469
-Hello, everyone,
and welcome back to the attic.

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:04.804
I want to take a quick second
to address something

00:00:04.804 --> 00:00:06.606
that was pointed out to me
over the weekend.

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:09.975
According to some
eagle-eyed Internet sleuths,

00:00:09.975 --> 00:00:13.680
the title of my trusted copy
of "The Thorn Birds" changed

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.181
over the course
of "A Closer Look."

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:17.283
Obviously the last thing
we want is for any book nonsense

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:19.218
to distract from the content
of "A Look."

00:00:19.218 --> 00:00:20.953
So to make sure it doesn't
happen this week,

00:00:20.953 --> 00:00:25.124
I will be placing a book
on top of my copy

00:00:25.124 --> 00:00:26.926
of "The Thorn Birds"
to keep it in place,

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:29.896
and that right there should be
the end of that.

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:32.898
Also I want to note that it has
now been 70 days

00:00:32.898 --> 00:00:35.501
since my last haircut, and while
it looks tame enough now,

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:37.236
I assure you that
over the weekend,

00:00:37.236 --> 00:00:38.571
this thing is a hot mess.

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:41.141
So thank God for Monday
and a reason to comb it.

00:00:41.141 --> 00:00:43.176
Speaking of hot messes,
segue, it's clear.

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:45.578
The president desperately wants
to pretend the coronavirus

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:47.914
will just go away, and now
he's trying to distract

00:00:47.914 --> 00:00:49.349
from his own
poor job performance

00:00:49.349 --> 00:00:52.018
by calling for his predecessor
to be investigated

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:54.454
for a made-up scandal
he can't even define.

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:57.156
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:57.156 --> 00:01:01.060 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:03.129
One of the most frustrating
parts of this pandemic

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:05.531
has been watching countries
around the world from Australia

00:01:05.531 --> 00:01:07.767
to Iceland to Taiwan
to New Zealand

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:09.735
successfully suppress
their outbreaks

00:01:09.735 --> 00:01:11.037
with competent leadership

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:13.406
and slowly begin to safely
reopen their economies.

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:16.242
Meanwhile, we have a president
who won't even wear a mask

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:18.410
at a mask-distribution facility

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:20.379
while surrounded by people
wearing masks.

00:01:20.379 --> 00:01:23.382
Oh, sure, when he was trying to
get everyone excited about coal,

00:01:23.382 --> 00:01:25.117
he happily put on
a miner's helmet.

00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:27.686
But at a time when experts are
begging people to wear masks,

00:01:27.686 --> 00:01:30.356
he stands there like a science
experiment being unveiled

00:01:30.356 --> 00:01:31.925
by a bunch of doctors
at a conference.

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:36.429
As you can see, we successfully
implanted the brain of a pigeon

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:39.999
into a giant potato
and then sewed on some limbs

00:01:39.999 --> 00:01:42.835
and shocked it with electricity
until it came to life.

00:01:42.835 --> 00:01:45.305
So, you know,
still working out some kinks.

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:46.872
Dude, seriously,
just wear a mask.

00:01:46.872 --> 00:01:49.209
I promise it won't make you
look less presidential

00:01:49.209 --> 00:01:51.411
because there's no way
you could look

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:53.145
less presidential
than you do now.

00:01:53.145 --> 00:01:55.414
Do you think we're going to be
bummed out to be deprived

00:01:55.414 --> 00:01:57.082
of this part of the face?

00:01:57.082 --> 00:02:00.219
Not only have many countries
suppressed their outbreaks,

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:03.489
they've also avoided the
worst-case economic scenarios.

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:05.091
Meanwhile here in the U.S.

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:07.360
we now account for 30%
of the world's cases

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:10.430
despite having less than 5%
of the world's population.

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:12.298
36 million people
are out of work.

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:14.900
We have the highest unemployment
rate since the Great Depression.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:17.637
And last week the Fed reported
that a staggering

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:21.306
40% of households
making $40,000 or less

00:02:21.306 --> 00:02:22.575
lost their jobs in March,

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:25.044
or as the president
put it last week...

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:28.280
-We have met the moment
and we have prevailed.

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.416
-Mr. President, you said in
your comments earlier,

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:32.986
"we have met the moment,
we have prevailed."

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:35.421
To you, sir, is the mission
accomplished?

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:37.923
Even with 1.4 million --
-No, we've prevailed on testing

00:02:37.923 --> 00:02:40.626
is what I was referring to.
That was with regard to testing.

00:02:40.626 --> 00:02:41.661
-[ As Trump ] Sorry,
I read that wrong.

00:02:41.661 --> 00:02:43.429
I didn't mean to say
"prevailed."

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:45.264
I meant to say "pre-failed."

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:48.467
We failed before we even knew
what we were failing at.

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:49.802
That's vision.

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:51.203
[ Normal voice ] You can't make
a big statement like

00:02:51.203 --> 00:02:53.939
"We've prevailed," then say
it's just on testing.

00:02:53.939 --> 00:02:57.210
It's like if George W. Bush's
infamous banner had an asterisk

00:02:57.210 --> 00:03:00.279
that said "Mission Accomplished,
specifically the mission

00:03:00.279 --> 00:03:02.214
of printing and hanging
this banner."

00:03:02.214 --> 00:03:04.583
Also, we have not prevailed
on testing.

00:03:04.583 --> 00:03:06.819
I mean, it's good that
we're ramping up testing now,

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:08.320
but we needed it
three months ago.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:11.190
Bragging about testing now
is like showing up to a house

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:13.392
that already burned down
and offering to water the grass.

00:03:13.392 --> 00:03:15.528
Other countries are putting
in place rigorous programs

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:18.531
of testing, contact tracing,
and isolating cases.

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:19.765
That's why they've been able

00:03:19.765 --> 00:03:22.001
to slowly reopen
and avoid the worst.

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:24.270
We've fallen behind not just
countries like South Korea,

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.939
Australia, and Germany, but
others you might not expect.

00:03:26.939 --> 00:03:28.908
-This is what the graph looks
like for the U.S.

00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:30.943
You see a sharp rise in cases

00:03:30.943 --> 00:03:33.179
that hasn't really tapered off
yet, right?

00:03:33.179 --> 00:03:34.547
It's trending down.

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:37.383
But to put that in context,
that curve you see there,

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:39.251
here's how some other places
are doing.

00:03:39.251 --> 00:03:41.354
The first group
is the countries that appear

00:03:41.354 --> 00:03:44.224
to have successfully suppressed
transmission of the disease.

00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:46.592
That curve has
come all the way down

00:03:46.592 --> 00:03:49.729
so that they are barely
registering any new cases.

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:54.767
We have Andorra, Australia,
Austria, Bhutan, Cambodia,

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:59.004
China, Croatia, Cuba, Djibouti,

00:03:59.004 --> 00:04:02.041
Estonia, Greece, Iceland,

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:05.411
Jamaica, Jordan, Kosovo,

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:09.181
Latvia, Lebanon, Liechtenstein,

00:04:09.181 --> 00:04:12.318
Lithuania, Luxembourg, Malta,

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:15.521
Mauritius, Monaco, Montenegro,

00:04:15.521 --> 00:04:19.358
New Zealand, Slovakia, Slovenia,

00:04:19.358 --> 00:04:23.295
South Korea, Taiwan, Thailand,

00:04:23.295 --> 00:04:26.265
Tunisia, and finally, Vietnam.

00:04:26.265 --> 00:04:29.702
-We're worse than Liechtenstein,
Slovakia, and Latvia.

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:32.405
I don't even know enough about
those countries to make a joke.

00:04:32.405 --> 00:04:34.707
I'll just assume everyone there
is named Gustav

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:36.576
and they chug Fanta
while riding mopeds?

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:38.244
Let us know if we got close.

00:04:38.244 --> 00:04:40.112
We even did worse than Bhutan.

00:04:40.112 --> 00:04:41.981
Just a side note here
about Bhutan --

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:43.616
What's up with their graph?

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:45.284
Everyone else has a nice
bell curve,

00:04:45.284 --> 00:04:48.187
and their chart looks like the
opening credits of "Frasier."

00:04:48.187 --> 00:04:51.057
I guess Bhutan figured out that
the cure for coronavirus is...

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:53.526
♪ Tossed salads
and scrambled eggs ♪

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:56.028
No, you're doing a show
in your attic!

00:04:56.028 --> 00:04:58.431
Anyway, the point is,
there are lots of countries

00:04:58.431 --> 00:04:59.865
that have suppressed
their outbreaks.

00:04:59.865 --> 00:05:02.034
And now some of them
are safely reopening

00:05:02.034 --> 00:05:04.003
in ways that are still
far off for us.

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:07.239
Like Germany, where professional
soccer returned this weekend,

00:05:07.239 --> 00:05:09.108
although with a slight twist.

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:11.711
-Germany could help provide
the playbook

00:05:11.711 --> 00:05:14.346
for the future of sports
in the United States.

00:05:14.346 --> 00:05:17.416
Today, the Bundesliga will make
a return to the soccer field.

00:05:17.416 --> 00:05:20.686
It's the first major sports
league in the world,

00:05:20.686 --> 00:05:22.087
along with Korean baseball,

00:05:22.087 --> 00:05:24.723
to return during
the coronavirus pandemic.

00:05:24.723 --> 00:05:28.360
The move comes as Germany
eases nationwide restrictions

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:30.663
after seeing a drop
in new cases.

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:34.967
-Cheers like these will also
fade away, along with fans,

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:36.769
banned for the rest
of the season.

00:05:36.769 --> 00:05:39.338
Still, there will be some fans
in the stands

00:05:39.338 --> 00:05:42.808
with supporters paying to have
cardboard cutouts of themselves

00:05:42.808 --> 00:05:44.409
sitting in the stadiums.

00:05:44.409 --> 00:05:46.411
-That's right, German soccer
fans are paying to have

00:05:46.411 --> 00:05:48.247
cardboard cutouts of themselves
in the stands.

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:49.882
It's such a German solution,

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:51.384
because it's so much more
efficient

00:05:51.384 --> 00:05:53.352
than actually going to a game
yourself.

00:05:53.352 --> 00:05:55.655
[ German accent ]
Sport is merely a diversion

00:05:55.655 --> 00:05:58.324
from the ceaseless
march of time.

00:05:58.324 --> 00:05:59.925
[ Normal voice ] Angela Merkel
is going to start doing that

00:05:59.925 --> 00:06:01.226
for meetings with Trump.

00:06:01.226 --> 00:06:02.995
[ As Trump ] You've been
a lot more amenable today.

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:04.663
I like the new Angela.

00:06:04.663 --> 00:06:06.199
[ Normal voice ]
Also, true story, side note,

00:06:06.199 --> 00:06:08.734
for mother's day,
my brother sent my mom

00:06:08.734 --> 00:06:10.536
a cardboard cutout of himself.

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:12.471
Oh, my God,
look how happy she is.

00:06:12.471 --> 00:06:13.939
An incredibly thoughtful gift

00:06:13.939 --> 00:06:17.343
that made my gift of flowers
with a note pale in comparison.

00:06:17.343 --> 00:06:18.644
I don't have a photo to show you

00:06:18.644 --> 00:06:20.045
because she didn't take
one of that.

00:06:20.045 --> 00:06:21.914
And to my brother,
I would just like to say,

00:06:21.914 --> 00:06:25.083
pandemics are not the time
to curry favor with Mom,

00:06:25.083 --> 00:06:26.551
to which I'm sure he would say,

00:06:26.551 --> 00:06:28.955
even in non-pandemic times,
I get thoughtful gifts,

00:06:28.955 --> 00:06:30.155
and you don't,
to which I would say,

00:06:30.155 --> 00:06:32.458
"Bud, I would love to have
this conversation,

00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:33.659
but I got to get back
to my "Look."

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:36.595
Now, obviously
there are lots of factors,

00:06:36.595 --> 00:06:38.130
and those countries are all
very different,

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:40.399
but at least some
of those countries

00:06:40.399 --> 00:06:43.135
have made strides in part
due to a national strategy

00:06:43.135 --> 00:06:44.370
of widespread testing,

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:46.505
tracing the contacts
of positive cases,

00:06:46.505 --> 00:06:47.906
and isolating those cases.

00:06:47.906 --> 00:06:51.477
Meanwhile, our president doesn't
even think testing works.

00:06:51.477 --> 00:06:53.078
-We've been doing testing
at a level

00:06:53.078 --> 00:06:54.646
that nobody's ever done it
before.

00:06:54.646 --> 00:06:57.149
We have the best testing
in the world.

00:06:57.149 --> 00:07:02.587
Could be the testing is,
frankly, uh, overrated.

00:07:02.587 --> 00:07:04.824
Maybe it is overrated.

00:07:04.824 --> 00:07:08.594
But whenever they start yelling,
"We want more, we want more,"

00:07:08.594 --> 00:07:10.463
you know, they always say,
"We want more, we want more,"

00:07:10.463 --> 00:07:11.831
'cause they don't want
to give you credit.

00:07:11.831 --> 00:07:15.868
Don't forget, we have more cases
than anybody in the world.

00:07:15.868 --> 00:07:18.103
But why?
Because we do more testing.

00:07:18.103 --> 00:07:20.072
When you test, you have a case.

00:07:20.072 --> 00:07:23.376
When you test, you find
something is wrong with people.

00:07:23.376 --> 00:07:26.045
If we didn't do any testing,
we would have very few cases.

00:07:26.045 --> 00:07:28.213
-That doesn't mean the cases
would magically go away.

00:07:28.213 --> 00:07:29.281
They would still be there.

00:07:29.281 --> 00:07:30.783
You just wouldn't know about
them.

00:07:30.783 --> 00:07:32.618
If the Olympics stopped
drug testing people,

00:07:32.618 --> 00:07:34.854
there would be fewer positives,
but a lot more cyclists

00:07:34.854 --> 00:07:37.523
who looked like Dolph Lundgren,
which might not be terrible.

00:07:37.523 --> 00:07:39.192
This is clearly a theme
for Trump.

00:07:39.192 --> 00:07:41.960
He would much rather the U.S.
just stopped testing people

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:43.929
so we could pretend
we don't have any cases.

00:07:43.929 --> 00:07:46.933
For example, when a West Wing
aide tested positive

00:07:46.933 --> 00:07:48.667
for coronavirus earlier
this month,

00:07:48.667 --> 00:07:51.003
Trump said it somehow proved
his theory

00:07:51.003 --> 00:07:52.571
that testing isn't important.

00:07:52.571 --> 00:07:57.242
-She tested, uh, very good
for a long period of time,

00:07:57.242 --> 00:07:59.311
and then, all of a sudden,
today she tested positive.

00:07:59.311 --> 00:08:02.047
So, uh, she tested positive
out of the blue.

00:08:02.047 --> 00:08:06.518
This is why the whole concept of
tests aren't necessarily great.

00:08:06.518 --> 00:08:08.053
The tests are perfect.

00:08:08.053 --> 00:08:09.922
But something can happen
between a test

00:08:09.922 --> 00:08:12.258
where it's good and then
something happens,

00:08:12.258 --> 00:08:15.460
and all of a sudden,
she was tested very recently

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:18.597
and tested negative,
and then today, I guess,

00:08:18.597 --> 00:08:20.766
for some reason,
she tested positive.

00:08:20.766 --> 00:08:23.569
-Oh, he's so close
to getting it.

00:08:23.569 --> 00:08:25.504
Sometimes it feels like
we as a nation

00:08:25.504 --> 00:08:27.172
are helping the dumbest kid
in school

00:08:27.172 --> 00:08:28.374
with his science homework.

00:08:28.374 --> 00:08:30.442
[ As Trump ]
She tested negative every time.

00:08:30.442 --> 00:08:32.144
[ Normal voice ]
Yes, yes, yes, good, go on.

00:08:32.144 --> 00:08:34.480
[ As Trump ]
Then today, she tested positive.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:36.482
[ Normal voice ] Ah, yes,
yes, yes. Which means...?

00:08:36.482 --> 00:08:38.217
[ As Trump ]
Well, something changed.

00:08:38.217 --> 00:08:39.452
[ Normal voice ]
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes.

00:08:39.452 --> 00:08:41.653
Now, what changed?

00:08:41.653 --> 00:08:43.121
[ As Trump ] I don't know.

00:08:43.121 --> 00:08:44.490
[ Normal voice ]
She has the virus!

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:47.392
That's what changed.
She has the virus now.

00:08:47.392 --> 00:08:49.295
He thinks the problem
with testing

00:08:49.295 --> 00:08:50.762
is that you can test negative,

00:08:50.762 --> 00:08:52.298
meaning you don't have
coronavirus,

00:08:52.298 --> 00:08:55.567
then one day, you test positive
because you caught coronavirus.

00:08:55.567 --> 00:08:58.604
[ As Trump ]
Smoke detectors are useless.

00:08:58.604 --> 00:09:00.972
They'll be quiet for years,
and then you finally feel

00:09:00.972 --> 00:09:03.775
safe enough to leave a candle
on top of a mattress,

00:09:03.775 --> 00:09:05.310
and they just start beeping
like crazy.

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:08.180
It's clear that Trump would much
rather simply pretend

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:11.383
coronavirus no longer exists
and go about doing

00:09:11.383 --> 00:09:13.652
all the other president stuff
he used to do on Friday,

00:09:13.652 --> 00:09:15.855
for example,
as the U.S. death toll

00:09:15.855 --> 00:09:18.424
climbed to 88,000,
Trump took time out of his day

00:09:18.424 --> 00:09:22.661
to commission a new flag for his
pet project, the space force.

00:09:22.661 --> 00:09:26.098
-So today we're here for
a very important --

00:09:26.098 --> 00:09:28.166
it's really an important
occasion

00:09:28.166 --> 00:09:30.035
because we're unfurling
the flag.

00:09:30.035 --> 00:09:31.670
So, why don't we go ahead
and do it?

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:33.739
Let's do it, yes, please.
-Thank you.

00:09:33.739 --> 00:09:35.641
[ Camera shutters clicking ]

00:09:35.641 --> 00:09:38.177
[ Indistinct conversations ]

00:09:44.016 --> 00:09:45.951
-Look at that goon grinning
from ear to ear.

00:09:45.951 --> 00:09:48.454
He hasn't been that happy since
Prime had a two-for-one deal

00:09:48.454 --> 00:09:49.788
on gold toilets.

00:09:49.788 --> 00:09:52.591
I mean, compare that face
to the face he made the night

00:09:52.591 --> 00:09:54.293
he found out he was going
to be president.

00:09:54.293 --> 00:09:55.761
I would say he looks like
he just saw a ghost,

00:09:55.761 --> 00:09:57.630
but it was probably the one
he brought with him.

00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:59.998
So amid all of this,
former President Obama

00:09:59.998 --> 00:10:02.267
decided to offer some
rare public criticism

00:10:02.267 --> 00:10:05.104
during two virtual commencement
addresses over the weekend.

00:10:05.104 --> 00:10:06.238
Say what you will about him,

00:10:06.238 --> 00:10:07.707
he certainly had his flaws
as president,

00:10:07.707 --> 00:10:10.976
but it was so comforting
just to hear a politician

00:10:10.976 --> 00:10:13.712
capable of showing empathy
and compassion

00:10:13.712 --> 00:10:15.480
and talking in
coherent sentences.

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:18.217
-This pandemic has fully,
finally torn back the curtain

00:10:18.217 --> 00:10:21.320
on the idea that so many
of the folks in charge

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:23.455
know what they're doing.

00:10:23.455 --> 00:10:25.924
A lot of them aren't even
pretending to be in charge.

00:10:25.924 --> 00:10:29.094
And all those adults that
used to think were in charge

00:10:29.094 --> 00:10:31.296
and knew what they were doing,

00:10:31.296 --> 00:10:34.400
turns out they don't have
all the answers.

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:36.969
A lot of them aren't even asking
the right questions.

00:10:36.969 --> 00:10:41.039
Our society and our democracy
only work

00:10:41.039 --> 00:10:44.710
when we think not just about
ourselves, but about each other.

00:10:44.710 --> 00:10:48.213
Doing what feels good,
what's convenient, what's easy,

00:10:48.213 --> 00:10:50.215
that's how little kids think.

00:10:50.215 --> 00:10:52.484
Unfortunately a lot
of so-called grown-ups,

00:10:52.484 --> 00:10:55.054
including some with fancy titles
and important jobs,

00:10:55.054 --> 00:10:58.857
still think that way, which is
why things are so screwed up.

00:10:58.857 --> 00:11:01.259
-It's both revealing an
d depressing that when Obama

00:11:01.259 --> 00:11:03.495
talks about grown-ups behaving
like little children,

00:11:03.495 --> 00:11:05.898
we all know exactly
who he's talking about.

00:11:05.898 --> 00:11:08.133
I mean, there's no mystery.
Even Trump knows.

00:11:08.133 --> 00:11:10.202
It's not like his aides
went to him and said,

00:11:10.202 --> 00:11:12.004
"Sir, he was talking about you,
and Trump said,

00:11:12.004 --> 00:11:14.173
[ As Trump ] "Moi? But I was
just sitting here drawing

00:11:14.173 --> 00:11:17.410
a new logo for the space force.
Adult stuff.

00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:20.479
I think we can all agree,
adult stuff."

00:11:20.479 --> 00:11:23.782
Also I appreciate that Obama
did this, I really do,

00:11:23.782 --> 00:11:27.452
but as he himself acknowledged,
isn't like one of the upsides,

00:11:27.452 --> 00:11:30.622
maybe the only upside of having
your graduation canceled

00:11:30.622 --> 00:11:32.524
that you don't have to sit
through a long boring speech?

00:11:32.524 --> 00:11:34.894
I mean, don't get me wrong,
Obama is a great speaker,

00:11:34.894 --> 00:11:37.263
but instead of giving a speech,
maybe he could have hosted

00:11:37.263 --> 00:11:38.964
a game of virtual beer pong.

00:11:38.964 --> 00:11:42.367
[ As Obama ] That's two.
Two in a row. I get a rollback.

00:11:42.367 --> 00:11:46.738
Hey, there was too much space
between those cups.

00:11:46.738 --> 00:11:48.840
I want a re-rack.

00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:50.642
Better tighten that [bleep] up.

00:11:50.642 --> 00:11:52.210
Tighten it up.

00:11:52.210 --> 00:11:57.183
Obama's reemergence comes as
Trump pushes a totally deranged,

00:11:57.183 --> 00:12:00.152
made-up scandal
that even he can't define,

00:12:00.152 --> 00:12:01.721
but which he's already named

00:12:01.721 --> 00:12:04.090
in an attempt to distract
from coronavirus.

00:12:04.090 --> 00:12:07.259
And that dumb name has already
been parroted by the media.

